<div id="community-info" class="community-content">
  <section class="faq-section" id="faqs" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
    <div class="section-intro">
      <span class="eyebrow">A community looking out for you</span>
      <h2 id="faq-title">Before you share,<br>know how it works.</h2>
      <p>HerMap is built to help women make informed choices through community-reported experiences. Your privacy and your choice come first.</p>
      <div class="privacy-points"><span><?= ps_icon('user-shield') ?> No sign-up</span><span><?= ps_icon('heart') ?> Always free to report</span><span><?= ps_icon('lock') ?> Private review first</span></div>
      <a class="text-link" href="<?= ps_escape(ps_url('privacy-policy')) ?>">Read our privacy policy <?= ps_icon('arrow-right') ?></a>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details><summary>What is HerMap, and how can it help?</summary><p>HerMap is a free public-interest initiative for women in India. Its map shows broad patterns in reviewed community reports, helping people consider surroundings and journeys with more context. It is not an official crime map or a safety rating.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can I report an incident now?</summary><p>The local development service saves structured reports for private moderation when intake is enabled. Choose an experience, a broad location, date and approximate time in IST, then complete the human check. Your report does not appear publicly on submission. Public deployment is still being prepared.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Will I need to share my identity?</summary><p>No name, email, phone number, identity document or public account is required. This does not mean complete anonymity from hosting systems or lawful authorities. Please never include identifying details about yourself, a survivor or a child. The optional online account field is only for private context about the account involved in your experience.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Does HerMap save my information or track me?</summary><p>Submitted location, category, date, time and optional venue or online account details are saved privately. A point you explicitly choose to share is encrypted; device location is never attached automatically. A necessary session cookie protects forms. We count page visits and active visits using temporary random tokens, without visitor profiles, advertising or behavioural analytics. Hosting systems may still process request logs. See the <a href="<?= ps_escape(ps_url('privacy-policy')) ?>">privacy policy</a> for security rate limits and retention.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Will anything I report become public?</summary><p>Individual reports, exact times, receipt codes, venue names, account handles and exact coordinates are never shown on the map. Approved reports wait at least <?= PUBLICATION_DELAY_HOURS ?> hours; groups below <?= PUBLIC_MIN_REPORTS ?> reports are withheld. Eligible counts appear in bands of five within broad 0.25° grid cells. The overall received-report counter includes submissions before moderation.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can I add a venue or online account?</summary><p>Yes. These place types show optional organisation or public venue name and official website fields. Details are encrypted for private review and stay off the public map. For online harassment, an optional username and platform can also be provided for encrypted private review. Never include survivor or child identifiers, real names, room numbers or private addresses.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Do more reports mean a place is unsafe?</summary><p>More reports show more reporting activity, not proof that a place is unsafe. Population, awareness, duplicate attempts and coordinated misuse can affect counts. The maths check and moderation reduce misuse; they cannot prove that a report is genuine. No business is automatically labelled unsafe from a count.</p></details>
      <details><summary>How can I check or delete my report?</summary><p>Save the private receipt shown after submission. Use “Check or delete an existing report” in the reporting dialog. The receipt cannot be recovered if lost. Deletion removes the incident record and private venue/online/location details; non-identifying counters and review logs may remain. Anyone with the receipt can access these controls.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Will reporting always be free?</summary><p>Yes. Reporting will remain free, with no payment required to share an experience. Viewing the map is free too.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can HerMap send help or file a complaint?</summary><p>HerMap cannot dispatch emergency help, monitor urgent reports or file a police complaint. In immediate danger in India, <a href="tel:112">call 112</a>. The support links below connect you to official services for women’s support, online crime and workplace sexual harassment. Each service has its own process and privacy policy.</p></details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="support" class="support-section" aria-labelledby="support-title">
    <div class="support-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">Help beyond the map</span><h2 id="support-title">You deserve support.</h2></div><p>Official India helplines and reporting services. In immediate danger, call 112. HerMap is not an emergency service.</p></div>
    <div class="support-grid">
      <article class="support-card panel"><span class="support-icon"><?= ps_icon('phone') ?></span><span class="small-label">Immediate danger</span><h3>Emergency response</h3><p>For emergency police, fire or medical assistance in India.</p><a class="support-call" href="tel:112">Call 112 <?= ps_icon('arrow-right') ?></a><a class="support-source" href="https://112.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Official ERSS website <?= ps_icon('arrow-up-right-from-square') ?></a></article>
      <article class="support-card panel"><span class="support-icon"><?= ps_icon('hands-holding-circle') ?></span><span class="small-label">Support for women</span><h3>Women Helpline</h3><p>Connect with support and referrals to services including One Stop Centres. Availability varies by state; the Ministry currently lists West Bengal as an exception.</p><a class="support-call" href="tel:181">Call 181 <?= ps_icon('arrow-right') ?></a><a class="support-source" href="https://wcd.gov.in/women/help" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ministry helpline information <?= ps_icon('arrow-up-right-from-square') ?></a></article>
      <article class="support-card panel"><span class="support-icon"><?= ps_icon('shield-halved') ?></span><span class="small-label">Online harassment or crime</span><h3>National cybercrime portal</h3><p>Use the official portal to find the relevant cybercrime complaint route. Follow its instructions; identity requirements depend on the complaint type.</p><a class="support-call" href="https://cybercrime.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit cybercrime.gov.in <?= ps_icon('arrow-up-right-from-square') ?></a><a class="support-source" href="https://www.cybercrime.gov.in/Accept.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Official reporting guidance <?= ps_icon('arrow-up-right-from-square') ?></a></article>
      <article class="support-card panel"><span class="support-icon"><?= ps_icon('briefcase') ?></span><span class="small-label">Workplace sexual harassment</span><h3>SHe-Box</h3><p>The government’s complaint portal for sexual harassment at work, including public and private workplaces.</p><a class="support-call" href="https://shebox.wcd.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit SHe-Box <?= ps_icon('arrow-up-right-from-square') ?></a><a class="support-source" href="https://missionshakti.wcd.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ministry’s Mission Shakti portal <?= ps_icon('arrow-up-right-from-square') ?></a></article>
      <article class="support-card panel"><span class="support-icon"><?= ps_icon('credit-card') ?></span><span class="small-label">Financial cyber fraud</span><h3>Cyber fraud helpline</h3><p>For immediate reporting of online financial fraud. For online harassment without financial fraud, use the cybercrime portal above.</p><a class="support-call" href="tel:1930">Call 1930 <?= ps_icon('arrow-right') ?></a><a class="support-source" href="https://www.cybercrime.gov.in/Webform/Crime_NodalGrivanceList.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Official cybercrime information <?= ps_icon('arrow-up-right-from-square') ?></a></article>
      <article class="support-card panel"><span class="support-icon"><?= ps_icon('house-chimney-medical') ?></span><span class="small-label">In-person assistance</span><h3>One Stop Centres</h3><p>Find government support that can connect women experiencing violence with medical, legal and counselling services.</p><a class="support-call" href="https://missionshakti.wcd.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Find support through Mission Shakti <?= ps_icon('arrow-up-right-from-square') ?></a><a class="support-source" href="https://wcd.gov.in/women/help" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Women Helpline referrals <?= ps_icon('arrow-up-right-from-square') ?></a></article>
    </div>
    <p class="support-footnote">Sources checked on 10 October 2026. Services and availability may change; check the official websites for current guidance. Calls and external websites are handled by those providers under their own privacy policies. These links do not indicate a partnership or endorsement.</p>
  </section>
</div>
